<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Orinoco Belt</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/orinoco">Orinoco</a> Belt is a territory along the southern part of the eastern Orinoco River basin in Venezuela, about 600 km long, that holds one of the largest deposits of heavy and extra-heavy crude oil in the world. Its reserves make up most of Venezuela's proven reserves, the largest of any country. Its projects were nationalised under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hugo-chavez">Hugo Chávez</a> in 2007, when foreign companies had to accept majority control by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/petroleos-de-venezuela">PDVSA</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/orinoco-belt.jpg" alt="Orinoco Belt" width="320" height="272" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: USGS · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Orinoco_USGS.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
